      "id": "sol.amc-12b-fall-2021-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Write \\(n = 8^{2022} = 2^{6066}.\\) Then \\[\\dfrac{n}{4} = \\dfrac{2^{6066}}{2^{2}} = 2^{6064}.\\]\n\nSince \\(2^{6064} = 4^{3032},\\) this matches the last option.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite everything as a power of \\(2\\)",
        "\\(\\dfrac{n}{4} = \\dfrac{2^{6066}}{2^{2}}\\)"
      ],
